  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          ucode
  _item_default.value      NO
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
    YES
    NO
   save_

####################################
## PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_CONDITION ##
####################################

save_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _category.description
;  Data items in the PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_CONDITION category describe
   the WHEN, THEN and UNLESS conditions of a deposition rule. One record
   per condition.

   Roles:
     WHEN    the rule applies only if the WHEN conditions hold.
     UNLESS  the rule does not apply if the UNLESS conditions hold.
     THEN    the requirement checked when the rule applies.
   A violation is reported when the WHEN conditions hold, the UNLESS
   conditions do not hold, and the THEN conditions fail.
   If a rule has no WHEN condition, it applies to every scope row.
   If a rule has no UNLESS condition, no scope row is exempted.
   A rule with neither WHEN nor UNLESS conditions therefore checks its
   THEN conditions for every scope row. Every rule except procedural
   rules must have at least one THEN condition.

   Conditions with the same role in a rule are combined using
   _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.group_operator. All conditions with
   the same role in a rule must use the same group operator.

   Evaluation:
   Each rule is evaluated separately for each row of the rule's scope
   category (_pdbx_deposition_rule.scope_category). Evaluation proceeds
   in this order:
     (1) rows of each category referred to by the rule are restricted
         as defined in PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_ROW_SELECTION;
     (2) each remaining scope row is paired with rows of each partner
         category as defined in PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_JOIN; if no join
         is defined, every row of the partner category is a partner of
         every scope row;
     (3) the conditions are evaluated for the scope row; a condition
         that refers to a partner category is evaluated over the
         partner rows paired with that scope row, using
         _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.quantifier. Each condition is
         quantified independently. If
         _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.value_transform is given, it
         is applied to the item values before they are compared.
   Each failing scope row is reported as a separate violation.

   Categories:
     - The items in a single condition may belong to the scope
       category and at most one partner category.
     - If one item of a condition belongs to the scope category and
       the other to a partner category, the scope item is given in
       item_name and the partner item in compare_item_name.
     - WHEN, THEN and UNLESS conditions: item_name may belong to the
       scope category or to a partner category. compare_item_name may
       belong to:
         the scope category, when item_name also belongs to the scope
           category (both values are taken from the scope row);
         a partner category, when item_name belongs to the scope
           category (the scope value is compared with each partner
           row);
         the same partner category as item_name (both values are
           taken from the same partner row).
       compare_item_name may not belong to the scope category when
       item_name belongs to a partner category; swap the two items and
       use the reverse operator instead (e.g. LE_ITEM for GE_ITEM).
     - For the IN_COLUMN_OF operator, compare_item_name refers to the
       values of that item in all rows of its category remaining after
       row selection; joins and the quantifier do not apply to it.
     - For the IN_ENUMERATION_DETAILS_OF operator, compare_item_name
       must belong to the same category as item_name, and its value is
       taken from the same row. That value is looked up among the
       values enumerated for compare_item_name in the main dictionary
       (_item_enumeration.value or _pdbx_item_enumeration.value). The
       detail of the matching entry (_item_enumeration.detail or
       _pdbx_item_enumeration.detail) is a comma-separated list of the
       values allowed for item_name, and the value of item_name must
       be one of them. Values are compared without regard to case when
       item_name has a case-insensitive type (e.g. ucode, uline). If
       the value of compare_item_name is not enumerated, or its entry
       has no detail, the comparison is skipped as for a missing value.
       Joins and the quantifier do not apply.
     - Procedural rules may have no THEN condition; the item checked
       is then given in PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_PARAM.

   Missing values:
   A value is missing if the item or its category is absent from the
   data, or if the value, after leading and trailing whitespace is
   removed, is empty, '?' or '.'. A value that cannot be
   interpreted according to its item type in the main dictionary is
   reported by dictionary validation and treated as missing here.
     - The operators EXISTS, NOT_EXISTS, EMPTY and NOT_EMPTY test for
       missing values and are evaluated normally. Over partner rows,
       every paired partner row is tested, including rows with missing
       values. If there are no partner rows, for example because the
       partner category is absent, a condition with quantifier ANY does
       not hold and a condition with quantifier ALL holds.
     - For all other operators (comparisons such as EQ, IN, MATCHES,
       GE or GE_ITEM), a comparison cannot be made if the value of
       item_name is missing, or, for operators that compare two items
       (EQ_ITEM, LE_ITEM, GE_ITEM, LT_ITEM, GT_ITEM), if the value of
       compare_item_name is missing. The comparison is then skipped:
         WHEN    the condition is treated as not holding, so the rule
                 does not apply to the row;
         UNLESS  the condition is treated as not holding, so the row
                 is not exempted;
         THEN    the condition is treated as satisfied, so no
                 violation is reported by this rule.
       Missing values are reported only by rules that test for them
       explicitly using NOT_EMPTY or EXISTS.
     - For comparisons evaluated over partner rows, partner rows with a
       missing value are ignored. If every partner row has a missing
       value, no comparison can be made and the condition is skipped
       as described above, whatever its quantifier: a WHEN or UNLESS
       condition is treated as not holding, and a THEN condition is
       treated as satisfied.
     - For IN_COLUMN_OF, missing values in the compare_item_name column
       are ignored.
     - For UNIQUE, rows with a missing value are excluded from the
       uniqueness check.
     - For aggregate rules, rows with a missing value are excluded
       from the aggregation.
     - A scope row with a missing value in any of its join items has
       no partner rows; _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.on_no_match
       applies.
     - Rows with a missing selector_item value are ignored by row
       selection (see _pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.selector).
;
  _category.id               pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _category.mandatory_code   no
  loop_
  _category_key.name        '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.rule_id'
                            '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.ordinal'
    loop_
    _category_group.id           'inclusive_group'
                                 'pdbx_group'
    loop_
    _category_examples.detail
    _category_examples.case
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
;
    Example 1
;
;
    loop_
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.rule_id
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.ordinal
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.role
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.item_name
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.operator
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.value
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.compare_item_name
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.group_operator
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.quantifier
    R001 1 WHEN '_exptl.method'                               EQ         'X-RAY DIFFRACTION' . . ANY
    R001 2 THEN '_diffrn_radiation_wavelength.wavelength'     NOT_EMPTY  .                   . . .
    R002 1 THEN '_pdbx_audit_revision_history.revision_date'  GE_ITEM    .                   '_pdbx_database_status.recvd_initial_deposition_date' . ALL
    R003 1 WHEN '_pdbx_initial_refinement_model.source_name'  EQ         PDB                 . . .
    R003 2 THEN '_pdbx_initial_refinement_model.accession_code' MATCHES  '^[0-9][A-Za-z0-9]{3}$' . . .
    R004 1 THEN '_atom_site.occupancy'                        LE         1.0                 . . .
    R006 1 WHEN '_em_support_film.material'                   NOT_EMPTY  .                   . . ANY
    R006 2 THEN '_em_sample_support.grid_type'                NOT_EMPTY  .                   . . .
    R007 1 THEN '_reflns.d_resolution_high'                   LE_ITEM    .                   '_refine.ls_d_res_high' . ALL
    R008 1 THEN '_refine_ls_shell.d_res_high'                 EQ_ITEM    .                   '_refine.ls_d_res_high' . ALL
    R009 1 THEN '_refine.ls_R_factor_R_free'                  LE_ITEM    .                   '_refine_ls_shell.R_factor_R_free' . ALL
;
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
    _pdbx_category_context.type         CONTRIBUTED
    _pdbx_category_context.category_id  pdbx_deposition_rule_condition

     save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.rule_id
    _item_description.description
;    A pointer to _pdbx_deposition_rule.id. 
; 
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.rule_id'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          code
  _item_linked.child_name  '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.rule_id'
  _item_linked.parent_name '_pdbx_deposition_rule.id'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.ordinal
    _item_description.description
;    An identifier for the rule condition.  
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.ordinal'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          int
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.role
    _item_description.description
;    Primary role for the rule condition. 
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.role'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          ucode
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
    WHEN
    THEN
    UNLESS
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.item_name
    _item_description.description
;    Full item name where the rule condition applies.
     Must be an item name defined in the main dictionary.
     The item may belong to the rule's scope category or to a partner
     category (see the PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_CONDITION category
     description).
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.item_name'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          code
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.operator
    _item_description.description
;    Operator for the rule condition.
     MATCHES_TYPE: the value of item_name must match the construct of
     at least one of the item types listed in value, given as a
     comma-separated list of _item_type_list.code values from this
     dictionary or the main dictionary. As in DDL2 type checking, the
     construct is a POSIX extended regular expression that must match
     the whole value.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.operator'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          ucode
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
  _item_enumeration.detail
    EXISTS                     "item_name is present in the data, whatever its value, including '?', '.', an empty string or whitespace"
    NOT_EXISTS                 'item_name is not present in the data'
    EMPTY                      "item_name is absent, or its value, with leading and trailing whitespace removed, is empty, '?' or '.'"
    NOT_EMPTY                  "item_name is present and its value, with leading and trailing whitespace removed, is not empty, '?' or '.'"
    EQ                         'value of item_name equals value'
    NE                         'value of item_name does not equal value'
    LT                         'value of item_name is less than value; numbers and dates are compared according to the item type'
    LE                         'value of item_name is less than or equal to value; numbers and dates are compared according to the item type'
    GT                         'value of item_name is greater than value; numbers and dates are compared according to the item type'
    GE                         'value of item_name is greater than or equal to value; numbers and dates are compared according to the item type'
    IN                         'value of item_name is one of the comma-separated values given in value'
    NOT_IN                     'value of item_name is none of the comma-separated values given in value'
    MATCHES                    'value of item_name matches the regular expression given in value'
    NOT_MATCHES                'value of item_name does not match the regular expression given in value'
    MATCHES_TYPE               'value of item_name matches the construct of at least one of the item types listed in value'
    EQ_ITEM                    'value of item_name equals the value of compare_item_name'
    LE_ITEM                    'value of item_name is less than or equal to the value of compare_item_name'
    GE_ITEM                    'value of item_name is greater than or equal to the value of compare_item_name'
    LT_ITEM                    'value of item_name is less than the value of compare_item_name'
    GT_ITEM                    'value of item_name is greater than the value of compare_item_name'
    UNIQUE                     'value of item_name occurs in only one row of its category'
    IN_COLUMN_OF               'value of item_name occurs among the values of compare_item_name in its category'
    IN_ENUMERATION_DETAILS_OF  'value of item_name is listed in the main dictionary enumeration detail for the value of compare_item_name in the same row'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.value
    _item_description.description
;    Value used by the rule condition.
     For IN and NOT_IN, a comma-separated list of values; for
     MATCHES_TYPE, a comma-separated list of item type codes. A single
     space after a comma is allowed and is not part of the next entry.
     A list entry cannot itself contain a comma.
     For MATCHES and NOT_MATCHES, a regular expression; for other
     comparison operators, a single value. For these operators a comma
     is part of the value.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.value'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          value_csv
  loop_
  _item_examples.case
   'X-RAY DIFFRACTION'
   'PDB'
   'ELECTRON MICROSCOPY,ELECTRON CRYSTALLOGRAPHY'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.compare_item_name
    _item_description.description
;    Full item name of the second item involved in the condition.
     Applies for cases where operators are *_ITEM, IN_COLUMN_OF and
     IN_ENUMERATION_DETAILS_OF.
     Must be an item name defined in the main dictionary.
     The item may belong to the scope category or to a partner
     category, as described in the PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_CONDITION
     category description. If it belongs to a partner category, its
     values are taken from the partner rows paired with the scope row
     (see PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_JOIN); if no join is defined, every row
     of the partner category is a partner of every scope row. For
     IN_COLUMN_OF, the item refers to the values in all rows of its
     category remaining after row selection, and joins do not apply.
     For IN_ENUMERATION_DETAILS_OF, the item must belong to the same
     category as item_name; its value in the same row selects the
     enumeration entry in the main dictionary whose detail lists the
     values allowed for item_name.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.compare_item_name'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          code
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.group_operator
    _item_description.description
;    Operator used to combine conditions with the same role (WHEN,
     THEN or UNLESS) in a rule. AND requires all of them to hold; OR
     requires at least one of them to hold. All conditions with the
     same role in a rule must use the same group operator.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.group_operator'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          ucode
  _item_default.value      AND
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
    AND
    OR
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.quantifier
    _item_description.description
;    Quantifier applied over the partner rows of the condition, i.e.
     the rows of the category of item_name or compare_item_name that
     is not the rule's scope category and that are paired with the
     current scope row (see PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_JOIN).
       ALL   condition must hold for every partner row
       ANY   condition must hold for at least one partner row
     If not given, the default is ANY for WHEN and UNLESS conditions
     and ALL for THEN conditions. The quantifier has no effect when
     both items belong to the scope category, when there is only one
     partner row, or for the IN_COLUMN_OF and IN_ENUMERATION_DETAILS_OF
     operators.
     Each condition is quantified independently; two ANY conditions
     on the same partner category may be satisfied by different
     partner rows.
     To require that a partner category is present, use EXISTS or
     NOT_EMPTY with quantifier ANY; with ALL, a condition over no
     partner rows holds.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.quantifier'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          ucode
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
  _item_enumeration.detail
    ALL   'condition must hold for every partner row'
    ANY   'condition must hold for at least one partner row'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.value_transform
    _item_description.description
;    Transformation applied to the values of item_name and, for
     operators that compare two items (*_ITEM), compare_item_name
     before the comparison is made. The literal value given in
     _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.value is not transformed.
     Applies only to items with a numeric type in the main dictionary.
     If not given, values are compared as they are.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.value_transform'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_condition
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          ucode
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
  _item_enumeration.detail
    ABS   'absolute value'
   save_

################################
## PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_PARAM ##
################################

save_pdbx_deposition_rule_param
  _category.description
;  The category provides name/value parameters for procedural and aggregate rules.
;
  _category.id               pdbx_deposition_rule_param
  _category.mandatory_code   no
  loop_
  _category_key.name         '_pdbx_deposition_rule_param.rule_id'
                             '_pdbx_deposition_rule_param.name'
  loop_
  _category_group.id         'inclusive_group'
                             'pdbx_group'
  loop_
  _category_examples.detail
  _category_examples.case
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
;
    Example 1
;
;
    loop_
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_param.rule_id
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_param.name
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_param.value
    R004 group_by   '_atom_site.pdbx_PDB_model_num,_atom_site.auth_asym_id,_atom_site.auth_seq_id,_atom_site.pdbx_PDB_ins_code,_atom_site.auth_atom_id'
    R004 aggregate  SUM
;
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
    _pdbx_category_context.type         CONTRIBUTED
    _pdbx_category_context.category_id  pdbx_deposition_rule_param

     save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_param.rule_id
    _item_description.description
;    A pointer to _pdbx_deposition_rule.id.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_param.rule_id'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_param
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          code
  _item_linked.child_name  '_pdbx_deposition_rule_param.rule_id'
  _item_linked.parent_name '_pdbx_deposition_rule.id'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_param.name
    _item_description.description
;    Name for the rule parameter.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_param.name'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_param
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          code
  loop_
  _item_examples.case
  _item_examples.detail
    aggregate
;   Aggregate rules: function applied to the rows of each group
    defined by group_by; the value SUM. The THEN condition is tested
    on the result.
;
    group_by
;   Aggregate rules: comma-separated list of item names, without
    spaces, whose values define the groups.
;
    source_category
;   Procedural rules: category providing the values to be checked
    (e.g. atom_site).
;
    target_category
;   Procedural rules: category the source values are checked against
    (e.g. entity_poly_seq).
;
    missing_message
;   Procedural rules: message reported when a source value has no
    counterpart in the target category.
;
    experiment_code
;   Code-gated rules: the rule applies only when this accession code
    type (e.g. PDB) is requested for the entry.
;
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_param.value
    _item_description.description
;    Value for the rule parameter. Lists of item names are
     comma-separated without spaces, as for item_name_csv.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_param.value'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_param
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          text
   save_

###############################
## PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_JOIN ##
###############################

save_pdbx_deposition_rule_join
  _category.description
;  Data items in PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_JOIN define how rows of the rule's
   scope category are paired with rows of a partner category. Used when
   _pdbx_deposition_rule.join_flag is YES. For each scope row, its
   partner rows are the rows of the partner category whose join item
   values are equal to those of the scope row. The number of partners
   per scope row (one-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-one, many-to-many)
   is inferred from the category keys in the main dictionary; when a
   scope row has more than one partner,
   _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.quantifier determines how the
   condition is evaluated.
   Each condition that refers to a partner category uses the join
   whose partner_item_names belong to that category; a rule may
   have at most one join per partner category.
;
  _category.id               pdbx_deposition_rule_join
  _category.mandatory_code   no
  loop_
  _category_key.name         '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.rule_id'
                             '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.ordinal'
  loop_
  _category_group.id         'inclusive_group'
                             'pdbx_group'
  loop_
  _category_examples.detail
  _category_examples.case
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
;
    Example 1 - R006: one-to-many join of em_sample_support to
    em_support_film. R007: one-to-many join of reflns to refine on a
    non-key item, with fallback to single-row pairing when the join
    items are absent. R008: many-to-one join of refine_ls_shell to
    refine. R009: one-to-many join of refine to refine_ls_shell,
    reduced to one partner by row selection.
;
;
    loop_
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.rule_id
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.ordinal
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.scope_item_names
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.partner_item_names
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.on_no_match
    R006 1 '_em_sample_support.id'           '_em_support_film.sample_support_id' SKIP
    R007 1 '_reflns.pdbx_diffrn_id'          '_refine.pdbx_diffrn_id'             SINGLE_ROW_FALLBACK
    R008 1 '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_refine_id' '_refine.pdbx_refine_id'             SKIP
    R009 1 '_refine.pdbx_refine_id'          '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_refine_id'    SKIP
;
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
    _pdbx_category_context.type         CONTRIBUTED
    _pdbx_category_context.category_id  pdbx_deposition_rule_join

     save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_join.rule_id
    _item_description.description
;    A pointer to _pdbx_deposition_rule.id.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.rule_id'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_join
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          code
  _item_linked.child_name  '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.rule_id'
  _item_linked.parent_name '_pdbx_deposition_rule.id'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_join.ordinal
    _item_description.description
;    An identifier for the join within the rule. A rule with conditions
     on more than one partner category has one record per partner
     category; every join starts from the rule's scope category.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.ordinal'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_join
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          int
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_join.scope_item_names
    _item_description.description
;    Comma-separated list (without spaces) of full item names in the rule's scope category
     whose values are matched against
     _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.partner_item_names, which belong to a
     partner category. More than one item defines a composite join:
     a scope row and a partner row are paired only if the values of
     every item pair are equal. The items need not be the category key.
     All items must belong to the same category. A rule with conditions
     on more than one partner category has one record per partner
     category. Must be item names defined in the main dictionary.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.scope_item_names'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_join
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          item_name_csv
  loop_
  _item_examples.case
    '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_refine_id'
    '_struct_ref_seq.align_id,_struct_ref_seq.pdbx_strand_id'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_join.partner_item_names
    _item_description.description
;    Comma-separated list (without spaces) of full item names in the partner category,
     matched position by position with
     _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.scope_item_names; the list must have the same
     length. The items need not be the category key. If they form the
     full key of the partner category, each scope row has at most one
     partner; otherwise a scope row may have several partners and
     _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.quantifier applies. All items must
     belong to the same category. Must be item names defined in the
     main dictionary.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.partner_item_names'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_join
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          item_name_csv
  loop_
  _item_examples.case
    '_refine.pdbx_refine_id'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_join.on_no_match
    _item_description.description
;    Action taken when a scope row has no partner row in the partner
     category, including when a join item of the scope row is missing.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_join.on_no_match'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_join
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          ucode
  _item_default.value      SKIP
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
  _item_enumeration.detail
    SKIP                 'the scope row is not evaluated'
    FAIL                 'the scope row is reported as a violation'
    SINGLE_ROW_FALLBACK  'if the join items are absent and each category has exactly one row, pair those rows; otherwise SKIP'
   save_

########################################
## PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_ROW_SELECTION ##
########################################

save_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _category.description
;  Data items in PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_ROW_SELECTION restrict the rows
   of a category on which a rule is evaluated, either by choosing one
   row (or one row per group) with the smallest or largest value of an
   item, or by keeping only rows that contain a value. Used when
   _pdbx_deposition_rule.row_selection_flag is YES. Rules are evaluated
   in this order: (1) row selection in each category, (2) pairing of
   rows as defined in PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_JOIN, (3) evaluation of
   WHEN / THEN / UNLESS conditions using
   _pdbx_deposition_rule_condition.quantifier. If a rule has no record
   here for a category, all rows of that category are evaluated.
;
  _category.id               pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _category.mandatory_code   no
  loop_
  _category_key.name         '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.rule_id'
                             '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.category_id'
  loop_
  _category_group.id         'inclusive_group'
                             'pdbx_group'
  loop_
  _category_examples.detail
  _category_examples.case
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
;
    Example 1 - R008: selection on the scope category (highest-resolution
    refinement shell compared with the overall refinement). R009:
    selection on the partner category (overall refinement compared with
    its highest-resolution shell).
;
;
    loop_
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.rule_id
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.category_id
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.selector
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.selector_item
    _pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.group_by
    R008 refine_ls_shell MIN '_refine_ls_shell.d_res_high' '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_refine_id'
    R009 refine_ls_shell MIN '_refine_ls_shell.d_res_high' '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_refine_id'
;
# - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
    _pdbx_category_context.type         CONTRIBUTED
    _pdbx_category_context.category_id  pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection

     save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.rule_id
    _item_description.description
;    A pointer to _pdbx_deposition_rule.id.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.rule_id'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          code
  _item_linked.child_name  '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.rule_id'
  _item_linked.parent_name '_pdbx_deposition_rule.id'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.category_id
    _item_description.description
;    Category whose rows are restricted. Usually the rule's
     _pdbx_deposition_rule.scope_category, but may be any other
     category referenced by the rule's conditions. Must be a category
     defined in the main dictionary.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.category_id'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          code
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.selector
    _item_description.description
;    Method used to choose the row within each group (see group_by).
     MIN selects the row with the smallest value of selector_item; MAX
     selects the row with the largest value. Rows where selector_item
     is missing ('?' or '.') are ignored. If several rows tie, all tied
     rows are kept. If no row qualifies in a group: when category_id is
     the rule's scope category, the rule is not evaluated for that
     group; when category_id is a partner category, the scope rows
     paired with that group have no partner and
     _pdbx_deposition_rule_join.on_no_match applies.
     ANY_VALUE keeps every row in which at least one item of
     category_id that is present in the data, other than those listed
     in exclude_items, has a value; rows without such a value are not
     evaluated. selector_item and group_by are not used with ANY_VALUE.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.selector'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _item.mandatory_code     yes
  _item_type.code          ucode
  loop_
  _item_enumeration.value
  _item_enumeration.detail
    MIN        'row with the smallest value of selector_item'
    MAX        'row with the largest value of selector_item'
    ANY_VALUE  'every row in which at least one item of category_id, other than those listed in exclude_items, has a value'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.selector_item
    _item_description.description
;    Full name of the item used to rank rows. Must belong to the category in
     _pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.category_id and must have a
     numeric type (e.g. int, float) or a date type (e.g. yyyy-mm-dd)
     in the main dictionary; values are compared according to that
     type. Text, code and range types are not allowed. To select the
     first or last row in a category, use an ordinal item
     (e.g. pdbx_ordinal) rather than row order in the file.
     Required when selector is MIN or MAX; not used with ANY_VALUE.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.selector_item'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          code
  loop_
  _item_examples.case
  _item_examples.detail
    '_reflns_shell.d_res_high'       'MIN selects the highest-resolution shell'
    '_reflns_shell.d_res_low'        'MAX selects the lowest-resolution shell'
    '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_ordinal'  'MIN selects the first listed shell'
    '_pdbx_audit_revision_history.revision_date'  'MAX selects the latest revision'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.group_by
    _item_description.description
;    Optional comma-separated list (without spaces) of items in the category that partition
     rows into groups; one row is selected within each group, e.g. one
     highest-resolution shell per dataset or per refinement. When the
     category is joined to another category through
     PDBX_DEPOSITION_RULE_JOIN, group_by should list the same items as
     the join so that selection is made per join group.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.group_by'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          item_name_csv
  loop_
  _item_examples.case
    '_reflns_shell.pdbx_diffrn_id'
    '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_refine_id'
   save_

save__pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.exclude_items
    _item_description.description
;    Optional comma-separated list (without spaces) of items in category_id that are
     ignored when selector is ANY_VALUE, e.g. key items that are
     filled in automatically. Not used with MIN or MAX.
;
  _item.name               '_pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection.exclude_items'
  _item.category_id        pdbx_deposition_rule_row_selection
  _item.mandatory_code     no
  _item_type.code          item_name_csv
  loop_
  _item_examples.case
    '_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_refine_id,_refine_ls_shell.pdbx_ordinal'
   save_
